        <briefdescription>
<para>Given a sign/zero extend instruction <computeroutput>Ext</computeroutput>, return the appropriate action to promote the operand of <computeroutput>Ext</computeroutput> instead of using Ext. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>NULL if no promotable action is possible with the current sign extension. <computeroutput>InsertedInsts</computeroutput> keeps track of all the instructions inserted by the other <ref refid="classanonymous__namespace_02_code_gen_prepare_8cpp_03_1_1_code_gen_prepare" kindref="compound">CodeGenPrepare</ref> optimizations. This information is important because we do not want to promote these instructions as <ref refid="classanonymous__namespace_02_code_gen_prepare_8cpp_03_1_1_code_gen_prepare" kindref="compound">CodeGenPrepare</ref> will reinsert them later. Thus creating an infinite loop: create/remove. <computeroutput>PromotedInsts</computeroutput> maps the instructions to their type before promotion. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
